Debugging:
  Thankfully, most of the bugs I had were because I derefrenced the wrong pointers.
  In order to confirm that I had freed all of the dynamically allocated memory, 
  I set break points in both the read_titles and get_favorites functions. As well as the 
  free_memory function. I then used the watch command I found in beej's GDB guide under hardware watchpoints
  to follow my pointers through the program, specifically, *book_ptr and *favorites_ptr so I could watch the 
  first pointer. Once I saw that the values were being freed, I could make an assumption that my code would pass the
  Valgrind test.
